 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Perfect. Once, during a full moon, a brave hunter went alone into the dark forest. Moonbeams cast shadows that move on their own, and hoot owls from the trees. He shot his arrow, and it found a deer. No, he's hunter, and he knew what he was doing. He skinned and packed the deer without its light showing him in the face. Totally true. The dark side of the skin shows you which way the arrow came from. Exactly the reaction I was aiming for. It teaches them little about night hunting too. Sure. Why did the tomato turn red? Because it realized it was being watched all the time. A ha only, kids love something about a silly reason.",
